{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he shall be cut off, etc.</b> One must give a reason why the punishment of a priest who eats consecrated foods outside their appointed time should be more severe — obligating karet — than one who eats carrion, torn flesh, and abominations. Know that from the very same reason they stated (Bava Metzia 114a): ״Israel defiles by tent, but a non-Jew does not defile by tent״ — it is because Israel are of the aspect of holiness, and therefore when the holiness departs from them, all the klipot gather together and come upon him. And this is the very reason in the matter before us: for since the consecrated foods are at a level beyond which there is no higher, when the time that HaShem commanded for them passes, the holiness departs and a great impurity settles upon them, which cuts off the soul of the one who eats it — unlike the impurity of eating other prohibitions such as carrion, torn flesh, abominations, etc., in which that impurity has no power to cut off the soul, and it is purified by lashes." "And the verse's saying <b>for he has profaned HaShem's holy thing</b> — which appears to be concerned about the flesh of the holy offering — according to our words it is concerned about the soul of the one who eats a thing of impurity. Or perhaps, since through the eating of the flesh he completes the act of the shelamim offering, therefore when they eat the flesh this constitutes a profanation of the holy offering — for he thereby completes what had already been accomplished through this act, and it is impure flesh, and it profanes what had already entered into the holy offering through the blood and the fats. And this too is a reason for the settling of a great impurity upon that flesh, for the aspect of evil hopes for and aspires to a place entangled with and attached to holiness."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:58:53.022323427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}